AUDIO: 'The animation is already finished, but the client suddenly wants a different version. What do you do? With hundreds of keyframes already in place, directly editing the original animation can easily mess up the existing motion. Blender\'s NLA editor allows you to layer'

[00:13] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The Blender NLA editor is displayed, showing tracks for "BritishShorthair_Body" and "BritishShorthair_Eye". The NLA editor shows an action strip named "BritishShorthair_Stretch". The NLA editor with the "BritishShorthair_Stretch" action strip highlighted. The NLA editor with the "BritishShorthair_Stretch" action strip and an "Action" panel open. The NLA editor with the "BritishShorthair_Stretch" action strip and an "Action" panel open.
AUDIO: 'new animation on top of your existing motion. First, push the original animation down into the NLA editor, then create a new action and set the blend mode to combine.'

